error[E0277]: the terms `(EqualityTerm, MatchTerms)` do not answer the operator through exactly one term
  --> tests/ui/marker_tuple_operator_not_answered.rs:26:37
   |
26 |     let _ = EncryptedUser::EMAIL.gt("ada@example.com");
   |                                  -- ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ their answers are `(No, No)`
   |                                  |
   |                                  required by a bound introduced by this call
   |
   = help: the trait `AnsweredBy<(No, No)>` is not implemented for `(EqualityTerm, MatchTerms)`
   = note: a tuple of terms answers an operator when exactly one of its terms does: here none does, or several do
   = help: the following other types implement trait `AnsweredBy<Answers>`:
             `(A, B)` implements `AnsweredBy<(No, Yes)>`
             `(A, B)` implements `AnsweredBy<(Yes, No)>`
             `(A, B, C)` implements `AnsweredBy<(No, No, Yes)>`
             `(A, B, C)` implements `AnsweredBy<(No, Yes, No)>`
             `(A, B, C)` implements `AnsweredBy<(Yes, No, No)>`
             `(A, B, C, D)` implements `AnsweredBy<(No, No, No, Yes)>`
             `(A, B, C, D)` implements `AnsweredBy<(No, No, Yes, No)>`
             `(A, B, C, D)` implements `AnsweredBy<(No, Yes, No, No)>`
           and $N others
   = note: required for `(EqualityTerm, MatchTerms)` to implement `Answers<stack_encrypt::op::Gt, _>`
   = note: 1 redundant requirement hidden
   = note: required for `Encrypted<(EqualityTerm, MatchTerms)>` to implement `Answers<stack_encrypt::op::Gt, _>`
note: required by a bound in `Marker::<W, T, C, P>::gt`
  --> src/marker.rs
   |
   |                   T: Answers<$op, Q::Value> + LabelledTarget,
   |                      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ required by this bound in `Marker::<W, T, C, P>::gt`
...
   | / operator_methods! {
   | |     /// Rows whose value equals `value` ([`op::Eq`](struct@Eq)).
   | |     eq => Eq;
   | |     /// Rows whose value is below `value` ([`op::Lt`](Lt)).
...  |
   | |     gt => Gt;
   | |     -- required by a bound in this associated function
...  |
   | |     matches => Matches;
   | | }
   | |_- in this macro invocation
   = note: this error originates in the macro `operator_methods` (in Nightly builds, run with -Z macro-backtrace for more info)

